CACHE_BUST_ID: 2026-03-18-critical-fix

This file forces Railway to invalidate all Docker layer caches
and rebuild from scratch. It solves the issue where Railway
was using stale compiled code from old deployments.

Issue: DATABASE_URL not being read from environment variables
because Docker image had hardcoded localhost fallback from
development code that should have been removed.

Solution: Force complete Docker rebuild by adding this marker file.
Railway's buildpack system will detect the file change and
rebuild all layers from scratch, ensuring:
- Fresh npm install (node_modules)
- Recompiled TypeScript (dist/)
- Latest environment variable resolution
- No cached development code

All recent fixes are now included:
- Image combining logic (e6dcabd)
- JSON parsing for existing images (e3b2839)
- Docker cache invalidation triggers
